<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kindattu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 2004 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century-bce">21st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kindattu was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimashki-dynasty">Shimashki dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>. Around 2004 BCE he sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a> and captured the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a>, ending Mesopotamian hegemony over Elam. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> treat this as the first major offensive achievement of Elamite military power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kindattu.jpg" alt="Kindattu" width="269" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dfg13 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lament_for_ur_(cropped).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
